<title>USA: CSCE board elects Adolph Reinhardt as chairman.</title>
<headline>CSCE board elects Adolph Reinhardt as chairman.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Coffee, Sugar and Cocoa Exchange (CSCE) said Tuesday its Board of Managers elected Adolph Reinhardt as chairman for a two-year term.</p>
<p>Reinhardt, of Reinhardt &amp; Merz, Inc, began his career at the CSCE in 1957 as a clerk. In addition to being a long-term member of CSCE and serving on its Board of Managers for over 21 years, Reinhardt is a member of the New York Cotton Exchange (NYCE) and was NYCE chairman for three years.</p>
<p>((-- New York Commodity Desk, +1 212 859 1640))</p>
